# Configurable N-to-1 Multiplexer (FPGA)

## Overview
Parameterized multiplexer implemented in Verilog HDL with configurable data width and selector depth, synthesized on Xilinx Vivado.

## Specs
- Configurable: N-bit data width, M selector bits (2^M inputs)
- Supported configurations: 2:1, 4:1, 8:1, 16:1 with 8/16/32-bit data
- Propagation delay: 0.84 ns (4:1, 16-bit, -3 speed grade)
- Resource usage: 4:1 MUX = 4 LUT6 (16-bit data), 8:1 MUX = 8 LUT6
- Implementation: Structural with generate blocks and ternary operator ? :

## Files
| File | Description |
|------|-------------|
| mux_nto1.v | RTL Design (Verilog 2001) - Parameterized module with generate block for scalable implementation |
| mux_nto1_tb.v | Simulation Testbench - Exhaustive verification for 2:1, 4:1, 8:1 configurations with random stimulus |
| mux_nto1.xdc | Timing & Pin Constraints (Basys3) - Input/output port mapping to FPGA switches and LEDs |
| mux_synthesis_report.txt | Resource utilization report showing LUT/FF usage per configuration |

## Tools
- Xilinx Vivado 2025.2
- Target Board: Digilent Basys3 (XC7A35T)
- Simulation: Vivado Simulator (xsim) with 1000ns test duration

